u eventually cave crack  down  and over consume more calories than if  you actually stuck to the plan  yep that again is why i always say  one of the best predictors of a binge is  restriction  let's see what else he has to say big  one huge one  do not lose weight too fast so many  people  they'll start a diet and lose like 25  pounds the first month  yeah it's motivating because you see the  scale weight dropping so quick and you  think you're doing amazing  you're losing muscle muscle burns  calories muscle makes your metabolism  higher yep pretty much  and this my friends is why i say  crash diets do not work  let's see what else eating too strict  cutting out food groups and stuff going  keto  saying oh i can only eat chicken rice  and broccoli  chicken tilapia and some fish and  cutting out all sweets  all junk all yummy delicious foods in  your whole life  that doesn't work long term it might  work short term  if you have extreme discipline you might  be able to follow that diet for a little  while  i could probably do it but i'm very very  uh  motivated to reach my goals but even i  wouldn't want to do it long term  why do that when you can have balance  balance is not all  or nothing balance is eating healthy but  still having some foods you like  okay so i want to preface this by saying  greg and i  may have different ideas about what  constitutes fun foods and balance  so while egg white french toast and  anabolic ice cream and popcorn  may be fun for greg for others they may  just be kind of like healthified  versions of  junk food still tasty and fun but  potentially not a full replacement for  moderate portions  of the real deal what i do 100 agree  with is the sentiment that if you are  bored as [ __ ]  eating the same bland chicken and sweet  potato meal prep dinner  you are not going to keep it up  again greg obviously loves popcorn and  his anabolic ice cream and things like  that  so if having these foods in his diet  every day  makes it sustainable and enjoyable for  him to still  meet his nutritional goals amazing  but i also want to clarify that getting  out of that all or nothing mentality  can also take the form of the flexible  and varied approach  that other youtubers were suggesting you  know different people will respond to  different levels of flexibility  and routine that is totally a personal  thing i think the take-home message here  is that  you don't have to take on a punishing  regime  that has you avoiding all the foods that  you enjoy  in favor of foods that you kind of hate  obviously there are some things that  greg suggests that i don't necessarily  side with  and sometimes the things that he does  himself are different than  what he suggests others do but i do get  why that is since he himself says that  he's got very specific fitness goals  and he's a lot more disciplined and  motivated than he acknowledges  most people to be very true so of course  a big reminder that even when an  influencer knows what they're talking  about  greg or myself included what they do  themselves may not be beneficial to you  in your health journey so folks to sum  it up you are probably seeing some  general trends in the information that  i've chosen to highlight in this  super top level summary here so to recap  here are my thoughts it's my opinion  that you will not sustain any weight  loss diet  or lifestyle that encourages severe  physical restriction a feeling of  emotional  scarcity or deprivation demonizing foods  or food groups  or barriers for you to enjoy your damn  life sure you might lose some weight but  you will gain it  right back when you drop that  restrictive diet and start eating  normally again  and actually we know that this weight  cycling pattern  is arguably more dangerous from a  metabolic perspective  than just never losing the weight in the  first place  so in order to have a shot at changing  your behaviors and your eating patterns  in the long run with the potential  outcome of weight loss  we really need to bring it back to  basics  so that means number one adding more  fruits and veggies to your diet  fruits and veggies are rich in situating  fiber energizing carbs  and are naturally lower in calories this  does not however mean  subsisting off of fruit and veggies  alone to reach your weight loss goals  to the point where it's displacing other  healthy foods and that brings me to my  next point  number two eating adequate sources of  lean protein  and healthy fats both of which are  important for satiety  and overall nutrition and the former for  maintaining metabolically active muscle  mass  number three including movement in your  day that's enjoyable  and sustainable including some  resistance training  which will help to build muscle mass and  support your metabolism  it does not need to be an extreme gym  session to count but  try to be as active as you can without  encroaching on  other enjoyable parts of your life so  it's a general rule of thumb  anywhere between 30 to 60 minutes of  movement a day  doing something that makes you feel good  can have both physical  and mental benefits number four avoiding  extreme behaviors like completely  restricting foods or food groups that  you  love eating too little exercising too  much  skipping meals when you're hungry etc  remember that both  physical deprivation and emotional  scarcity  can both set you up for a binge number  five  think moderate deficit not denial  on a very primitive mathematical level  yes  losing weight requires that you burn  more calories than you consume  period is it that simple no not at all  because  there are a lot of compensatory  mechanisms at play that can make this  a minus b equation not always perfectly  equal  c however whether you choose to count  calories manage portion sizes  or aim to eat more lower calorie higher  fiber voluminous fruits and veggies to  kind of edge out some of those higher  calorie snacks  find a way to make small changes to your  overall intake  without triggering a sense of  deprivation  once we cross that line with extreme  cleanses or fast or cutting out whole  food groups that we love  the trust is broken and the diet  generally fails ultimately you want to  make the  diet fit the person not fit the person  to the diet  so be gentle with yourself honor your  needs  and make it work for you in a way that's  sustainable  and doesn't make you feel deprived and  finally  consider the holistic picture yes  nutrition is arguably the most important  piece in the weight loss puzzle  exercise being second but these things  do not happen  in a vacuum and when i worked clinically  we used to always say  that it is never just about the food  there are so many other external factors  that are at play  that can influence our ability to reach  our weight loss goals  whether that's genetics food security  income or physical environment stress  anxiety etc so focus  on the things that you can control with  the resources that you  do have and also make sure to take care  of the things that go beyond just  physical activity and nutrition so  things like  taking care of your emotional health  getting enough sleep  managing stress and addressing emotional  eating triggers  unfortunately there is nothing  sensationalized or sexy about this  this is all just basic nutrition 101  and it just takes a little education a  lot of practice  and your own innate intuition to truly  get it  so shout out to the weight loss creators  that i highlighted today for sifting  through some of the noise  a reminder that i may not agree with  everything and that means i still want  all of you to approach  each of these channels with a critical  lens  ultimately not every message is going to  be supportive to  every person and their relationship with  food and their body  but my goal here was to highlight  through other youtubers  what i perceive to be the most likely  information  to inspire long-term change so that is  all today thanks again to buildbar for  sponsoring this video  let me know in the comments if you liked  it and you want to see more videos like  this  if you did of course subscribe to the  channel give it the thumbs up  and i will see you next time on abby's  kitchen bye  you
 

